-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Giri</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Doubrovin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ponomarev</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerald</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Blasberg</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Massague</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinct organ-specific metastatic potential of individual breast cancer cells and primary tumors</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>2005</year><volume>115</volume><fpage>44</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15630443</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kauffman</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>Stadler</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sokoloff</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rinker-Schaeffer</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metastasis suppression: the evolving role of metastasis suppressor genes for regulating cancer cell growth at the secondary site</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2003</year><volume>169</volume><fpage>1122</fpage><lpage>1133</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12576866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Steeg</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metastasis suppressors alter the signal transduction of cancer cells</article-title><source>Nat Rev Cancer</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12509767</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person